# Pins of fixed inputs that G takes itself (the oracle plan's N5;
# crates/moss-tests runtime_platform::private_checked_casts_preserve_chained_fixed_pin_meanings
# without the casts). F[] is fixed in T, U and V, which its result `q`
# mentions; G takes all three and binds them in a chain, each agreeing
# with the bind site (T = U = V = Old there). After the chain, G's `q` is
# `(a: U, b: V, c: Old)` in G's input terms, which every application reads
# as `(Old, Old, Old)`, the promised `q(T, U, V)` at the bind site.
# The pins are (T, U), (U, V) and (V, Old), each in G's input terms (a
# bind reads its type where it is made), and each agrees with main.
# Verdicts: oracle exit 0; native exit 0; Audit accepts since #95. Before,
# it rejected (`BTypeBind`: #71 protected a fixed input that G takes, so
# the body could not bind it; recorded in AUDIT-CHANGES #93). The
# disagreeing variant is pin-taken-chain-disagree.moss.
type T;
type U;
type V;
tag Old;
assume T, U, V { fn q(a: T, b: U, c: V); }
functor F[]: T, U, V -> q;
functor G: T, U, V -> q {
  bind T = U;
  bind U = V;
  bind V = Old;
  bind q = (a, b, c) => ();
}
fn main() {
  bind T = Old;
  bind U = Old;
  bind V = Old;
  bind F = G;
  bind F;
  q(Old, Old, Old);
}
